# Product Requirements Document

## Digital Crime Investigation Simulator ("CaseFile") — v2, OOP-Complete C++ Edition

Full-stack version: vanilla HTML/CSS/JS frontend, C++17/20 backend on the Crow framework, PostgreSQL database.

---

## 1. Problem Statement

CaseFile is a web-based digital crime investigation simulator that manages cases, suspects, witnesses, investigators, digital and physical evidence, and reports.

Version 2 is deliberately designed as a complete OOP-in-C++ showcase. Every concept in the course syllabus must appear in real, running backend code behind a Crow REST endpoint, not only in diagrams. The syllabus covers: the four pillars, classes/objects/constructors/destructors, all five inheritance types, overloading and overriding, virtual functions and abstract classes, operator overloading, exception handling, pointers and memory management, and multithreading with mutexes and deadlock.

## 2. Goals

- Implement every OOP concept listed in Section 5 in the C++ backend, with a traceable file, class and API for each.
- Build a complete full-stack web application with a native C++ backend using Crow.
- Provide a realistic crime-investigation workflow.
- Maintain evidence integrity using SHA-256 checksum verification.
- Be memory-safe and thread-safe, verified with AddressSanitizer, ThreadSanitizer and Valgrind.

**Non-goal:** the frontend demonstrates no OOP. All OOP lives in C++.

