## 11. Database Design (PostgreSQL)

**users**
`user_id` (SERIAL PK), `name`, `email` (UNIQUE), `password` (hashed), `role` (ENUM: ADMIN, INVESTIGATOR)

**cases**
`case_id` (SERIAL PK), `title` (UNIQUE), `description`, `status` (ENUM: OPEN, UNDER_INVESTIGATION, CLOSED), `priority` (INT), `created_date` (TIMESTAMP)

**evidence**
`evidence_id` (SERIAL PK), `case_id` (FK), `type` (ENUM: DIGITAL, PHYSICAL, TESTIMONIAL), `description`, `collected_by`, `hash` (TEXT), `metadata` (JSONB), `created_date`

**investigators**
`investigator_id` (SERIAL PK), `user_id` (FK), `specialization` (ENUM: CYBER, FIELD, TASK_FORCE), `availability` (BOOLEAN), `workload` (INT)

**case_assignments**
`case_id` (FK), `investigator_id` (FK), `assigned_date` (composite PK on both IDs)

**suspects**
`suspect_id` (SERIAL PK), `case_id` (FK), `name`, `details`

**audit_log**
`log_id` (SERIAL PK), `timestamp`, `thread_id`, `level`, `message`

**Notes:** use native ENUM types, foreign keys with `ON DELETE` / `ON UPDATE` policies, and transactions for multi-step writes such as assignment and transfer.

